ex, confirming T cell lineage identity across all T cell subpopulations. NCR1 (NKp46) and NCAM1 (CD56) confirm NK cell lineage identity. Together these markers define the T and NK cell compartment encompassing CD4\u207a, CD8\u207a, regulatory, MAIT, proliferating T cells, ILC3s, and CD56\u207aCD16\u207a and CD56\u207aCD16\u207b NK cell subtypes.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9", "10.57785/e9e1-wh09"], "markerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "NCR1", "NCAM1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "NCR1", "NCAM1"], "synonyms": ["unknown"], "categoryFullName": "lymphocyte", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000542", "categoryOntologyTerm": "lymphocyte", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}]}, {"name": "lvl3_cell_types", "description": "Level 3 cell type labels (most fine-grained).", "annotationMethod": "manual", "algorithmName": "NA", "algorithmVersion": "NA", "algorithmRepoUrl": "NA", "referenceLocation": "NA", "referenceDescription": "NA", "mode": "cell-labels", "status": "parsed", "labelCount": 13, "order": null, "labels": [{"name": "B cells", "count": 2676, "color": "#db5f57", "fullName": "B cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000236", "ontologyTerm": "B cell", "rationale": "MS4A1 (CD20) is a surface marker broadly expressed on mature B cells. CD79A is a component of the B cell receptor signaling complex and confirms B cell lineage identity. IGKC (immunoglobulin kappa constant) reflects active immunoglobulin expression characteristic of B cells. Together these markers reliably identify B cells and distinguish them from other lymphoid populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["MS4A1", "CD79A", "IGKC"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["MS4A1", "CD79A", "IGKC"], "synonyms": ["B lymphocyte", "B-lymphocyte", "B-cell"], "categoryFullName": "lymphocyte", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000542", "categoryOntologyTerm": "lymphocyte", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Plasma cells", "count": 393, "color": "#db9c57", "fullName": "plasma cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000786", "ontologyTerm": "plasma cell", "rationale": "JCHAIN (joining chain) is a component of polymeric immunoglobulins and is highly expressed in antibody-secreting cells. MZB1 (marginal zone B and B1 cell-specific protein) is an endoplasmic reticulum protein involved in immunoglobulin secretion, enriched in plasmablasts and plasma cells. Together these markers identify antibody-secreting plasma cells and distinguish them from naive and memory B cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9", "10.57785/e9e1-wh09"], "markerGenes": ["JCHAIN", "MZB1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["JCHAIN", "MZB1"], "synonyms": ["plasma B-cell", "plasma B cell", "effector B cell", "plasmocyte", "plasmacyte", "effector B-cell"], "categoryFullName": "B cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000236", "categoryOntologyTerm": "B cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "CD4\u207a T cells", "count": 13699, "color": "#dbd957", "fullName": "CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000624", "ontologyTerm": "CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell", "rationale": "CD3D and CD3E are components of the T cell receptor signaling complex, confirming T cell lineage identity. CD4 is a surface co-receptor defining the CD4\u207a T cell lineage. CD2 is a surface adhesion molecule broadly expressed on T cells and NK cells, supporting T cell activation. CD40LG (CD40 ligand) is expressed on activated CD4\u207a T cells and is involved in T cell-B cell interactions. Together these markers identify CD4\u207a T cells and distinguish them from CD8\u207a and regulatory T cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.57785/e9e1-wh09", "10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "CD2", "CD4", "CD40LG"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "CD2", "CD4", "CD40LG"], "synonyms": ["CD4-positive", " alpha-beta T-cell", " alpha-beta T lymphocyte", " alpha-beta T-lymphocyte"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000084", "categoryOntologyTerm": "T cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Cytotoxic CD8\u207a T cells", "count": 5246, "color": "#a0db57", "fullName": "CD8-positive, alpha-beta cytotoxic T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000794", "ontologyTerm": "CD8-positive, alpha-beta cytotoxic T cell", "rationale": "CD8A confirms CD8\u207a T cell lineage identity. PRF1 (perforin-1) and GZMB (granzyme B) are cytotoxic effector molecules stored in cytotoxic granules and are characteristic of cells with cytotoxic activity. CX3CR1 (fractalkine receptor) shows enriched expression in terminally differentiated cytotoxic T cells and is associated with effector memory and tissue-patrolling states. Together these markers identify cytotoxic CD8\u207a T cells and distinguish them from naive and memory CD8\u207a T cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.57785/e9e1-wh09", "10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["CD8A", "PRF1", "GZMB", "CX3CR1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD8A", "PRF1", "GZMB", "CX3CR1"], "synonyms": ["cytotoxic T cell", "killer T lymphocyte", "killer T-cell", "CD8-positive", " alpha-beta cytotoxic T-cell", "killer T-lymphocyte", "cytotoxic T-lymphocyte", "cytotoxic T-cell", " alpha-beta cytotoxic T lymphocyte", "cytotoxic T lymphocyte", "killer T cell", " alpha-beta cytotoxic T-lymphocyte"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000084", "categoryOntologyTerm": "T cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Memory CD4\u207a T cells", "count": 6161, "color": "#63db57", "fullName": "CD4-positive, alpha-beta memory T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000897", "ontologyTerm": "CD4-positive, alpha-beta memory T cell", "rationale": "CD4 is a surface co-receptor confirming CD4\u207a T cell lineage identity. LEF1 (lymphoid enhancer binding factor 1) is a transcription factor associated with memory T cell states. ITGB1 (integrin beta-1) is involved in T cell adhesion and tissue retention, with enriched expression in memory T cell populations. Together these markers identify memory CD4\u207a T cells and distinguish them from naive and effector CD4\u207a T cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.57785/e9e1-wh09"], "markerGenes": ["CD4", "LEF1", "ITGB1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD4", "LEF1", "ITGB1"], "synonyms": ["CD4-positive", " alpha-beta memory T lymphocyte", "T4.Mem.Sp", " alpha-beta memory T-lymphocyte", " alpha-beta memory T-cell"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000084", "categoryOntologyTerm": "T cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "CD8\u207a T cells", "count": 8431, "color": "#57db87", "fullName": "CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000625", "ontologyTerm": "CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell", "rationale": "CD3D and CD3E are components of the T cell receptor signaling complex, confirming T cell lineage identity. CD8A is a surface co-receptor defining the CD8\u207a T cell lineage and distinguishing these cells from CD4\u207a T cells. Together these markers reliably identify CD8\u207a T cells within the T cell compartment.", "rationaleDois": ["10.57785/e9e1-wh09", "10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "CD8A"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "CD8A"], "synonyms": ["CD8-positive", " alpha-beta T-lymphocyte", " alpha-beta T lymphocyte", " alpha-beta T-cell"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000084", "categoryOntologyTerm": "T cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Mucosal-associated invariant T cells", "count": 3117, "color": "#57dbc5", "fullName": "mucosal-associated invariant T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000940", "ontologyTerm": "mucosal-associated invariant T cell", "rationale": "CD3D and CD3E are components of the T cell receptor signaling complex, confirming T cell lineage identity. CD8A confirms a cytotoxic T cell co-receptor expression profile. KLRB1 (CD161) and SLC4A10 are enriched in mucosal-associated invariant T cells (MAITs) specifically, with SLC4A10 being a well-characterized MAIT cell marker involved in bicarbonate transport. Together these markers identify MAIT cells and distinguish them from conventional CD8\u207a and CD4\u207a T cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "CD8A", "KLRB1", "SLC4A10"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "CD8A", "KLRB1", "SLC4A10"], "synonyms": ["MAIT", "mucosal invariant T-cell", "mucosal-associated invariant T-lymphocyte", "mucosal invariant T cell"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000084", "categoryOntologyTerm": "T cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Treg cells", "count": 1412, "color": "#57b5db", "fullName": "regulatory T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000815", "ontologyTerm": "regulatory T cell", "rationale": "CD3D and CD3E are components of the T cell receptor signaling complex, confirming T cell lineage identity. FOXP3 is a transcription factor required for regulatory T cell specification and function, and is the defining marker of this population. TIGIT and CTLA4 are inhibitory receptors enriched in regulatory T cells, reflecting their immunosuppressive function. Together these markers reliably identify regulatory T cells (Tregs) and distinguish them from conventional CD4\u207a and CD8\u207a T cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "FOXP3", "TIGIT", "CTLA4"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "FOXP3", "TIGIT", "CTLA4"], "synonyms": ["suppressor T cell", "regulatory T lymphocyte", "regulatory T-cell", "suppressor T-cell", "Treg"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000084", "categoryOntologyTerm": "T cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "CD56\u207aCD16\u207a NK cells", "count": 5948, "color": "#5778db", "fullName": "CD16-positive, CD56-dim natural killer cell, human", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000939", "ontologyTerm": "CD16-positive, CD56-dim natural killer cell, human", "rationale": "NCR1 (NKp46) and NCAM1 (CD56) confirm NK cell lineage identity. GNLY (granulysin), PRF1 (perforin-1), and KLRD1 (CD94) reflect cytotoxic capacity broadly shared across NK cell populations. FCGR3A (CD16) defines the CD16\u207a subset and is involved in antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity. FGFBP2 and KLRF1 show enriched expression in this mature cytotoxic NK cell subset in adipose tissue single-cell datasets. Together these markers identify CD56\u207aCD16\u207a NK cells and distinguish them from CD16\u207b NK cell populations.", "rationaleDois": ["10.57785/e9e1-wh09", "10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["NCR1", "NCAM1", "GNLY", "KLRD1", "PRF1", "FCGR3A", "FGFBP2", "KLRF1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["NCR1", "NCAM1", "GNLY", "KLRD1", "PRF1", "FCGR3A", "FGFBP2", "KLRF1"], "synonyms": ["CD16-positive", " CD56-dim NK cell", "cytotoxic CD56-dim NK cell", "CD16+CD56+ NK cell", " CD56-low natural killer cell", " CD56-positive NK cell", " CD56-low NK cell", " CD56-positive natural killer cell", "cytotoxic CD56-dim natural killer cell"], "categoryFullName": "natural killer cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000623", "categoryOntologyTerm": "natural killer cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "CD56\u207aCD16\u207b NK cells", "count": 1432, "color": "#7357db", "fullName": "CD16-negative, CD56-bright natural killer cell, human", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:0000938", "ontologyTerm": "CD16-negative, CD56-bright natural killer cell, human", "rationale": "NCR1 (NKp46) and NCAM1 (CD56) confirm NK cell lineage identity. This population is defined by the absence of FCGR3A (CD16) expression, distinguishing it from the more cytotoxic CD56\u207aCD16\u207a NK cell subset. Together these markers identify CD56\u207aCD16\u207b NK cells within the broader NK cell compartment.", "rationaleDois": ["10.57785/e9e1-wh09", "10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9"], "markerGenes": ["NCR1", "NCAM1"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["NCR1", "NCAM1"], "synonyms": ["CD16-CD56bright NK cell", "CD16-negative", " CD56-bright NK cell", "CD56-bright cytokine secreting natural killer cell", "CD56-bright cytokine secreting NK cell"], "categoryFullName": "natural killer cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": true, "categoryOntologyTermId": "CL:0000623", "categoryOntologyTerm": "natural killer cell", "ontologyAssessment": null, "averageConfScore": null}, {"name": "Proliferating T cells", "count": 239, "color": "#b057db", "fullName": "cycling T cell", "ontologyTermExists": true, "ontologyTermId": "CL:4033069", "ontologyTerm": "cycling T cell", "rationale": "CD3D and CD3E are components of the T cell receptor signaling complex, confirming T cell lineage identity. MKI67 (Ki-67) is a marker of active cell proliferation. Together these markers identify a proliferating T cell population rather than a transcriptionally distinct T cell subset.", "rationaleDois": ["10.1038/s42255-025-01296-9", "10.1016/j.celrep.2018.06.110"], "markerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "MKI67"], "canonicalMarkerGenes": ["CD3D", "CD3E", "MKI67"], "synonyms": ["proliferating T cell"], "categoryFullName": "T cell", "categoryOntologyTermExists": tru